Scaffolding files (data.js, index.html, style.css, readme.md) are byte-identical to the upstream starter, and there are zero changes outside week5/. The only modified tracked file is week5/script.js; everything else in the diff is the new tests/ directory.

Now fix the density/sparsity terminology in run-real-pipeline.js. Current code:

```js
  // --- dataset shape & sparsity ---------------------------------------------
  const maxMovieId = movies.reduce((m, x) => Math.max(m, x.id), 0);
  const matrixCells = (numUsers + 1) * (maxMovieId + 1);
  console.log("\n== Dataset ==");
  console.log(`users=${numUsers} movies=${numMovies} ratings=${ratings.length}`);
  console.log(`dense matrix: ${numUsers + 1} x ${maxMovieId + 1} = ${matrixCells} cells`);
  console.log(`sparsity: ${(100 * ratings.length / matrixCells).toFixed(3)}% observed`);
```

Fix:
- conceptual matrix = numUsers × maxMovieId = 943 × 1682 (no sentinel)
- density = ratings / (943*1682) → report as density %
- sparsity = 1 - density → report as sparsity %
- model tensor shape [numUsers+1, maxMovieId+1] = 944×1683 including sentinel row/col 0 — report separately, clearly labeled as tensor allocation, not used for density.

Also move maxMovieId above (already is). Rewrite the block:

```js
  // --- dataset shape, density, sparsity --------------------------------------
  const maxMovieId = movies.reduce((m, x) => Math.max(m, x.id), 0);
  // The conceptual user-movie matrix is numUsers x maxMovieId (ids are 1-based;
  // the sentinel row/column 0 exists only because the factor matrices are
  // indexed by raw ids and must not count as a user or a movie here).
